The fixture is very small - just two files. Let me analyze the performance issues based on what I see.

The Coach/Program.cs has:
```
await critic.RunAsync(history, cancellationToken);
```

And HistoryHog.AppHost/Program.cs has:
```
var builder = DistributedApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.AddProject<Projects.Coach>("coach");
builder.AddProject<Projects.Critic>("critic");
builder.Build().Run();
```

The app is called "HistoryHog" which is a hint. The Coach program passes the entire `history` to `critic.RunAsync`. In multi-turn conversations, the history grows with each turn, and passing the full history every time would be increasingly expensive.
The real problem is that every turn sends the complete conversation history to the critic without any truncation or summarization, so the payload balloons as the conversation lengthens.
